================================================================================================
ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
================================================================================================
Do not force tournament vertices to be runners or arcs.
Useful vertices here include gaps, complements, interaction orders, local sinks,
observer charts, quotient debts, Hamiltonian spectra, and proof obligations.
The quotient preserves only the chosen predicate currency; it destroys the others.
